What is inflate — and how to debug it
What inflate actually is
inflate

is a placeholder deployment that runs pause containers — the lightest possible container (does nothing, uses ~0 CPU, ~1MB RAM). Its only job is to hold reserved capacity on nodes so that when a real workload arrives, a warm node is already available — no cold-start wait for Karpenter to provision one.

Without inflate:                    With inflate (correct):
─────────────────                   ──────────────────────────────
Real pod arrives                    Real pod arrives
    ↓                                   ↓
Karpenter provisions node           inflate pod gets EVICTED
    ↓ (~60-90 seconds wait)             ↓ (instant — node already warm)
Node joins cluster                  Real pod starts immediately
    ↓
